From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:40:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J: size the PiP window in floating point when it leaves
 full screen

PiPControlImpl.setFullScreen(false) gives the PiP window the size of the
secondary video relative to the screen as vd.width / sd.width and
vd.height / sd.height, an integer division: any secondary video smaller
than the screen (720x480 on 1920x1080, the usual PiP) gets a 0x0 area,
which getActiveVideoArea() and getFullScreen() then report to the Xlet.
Divide in floating point, as the other controls do.

Found while looking for other slips of the kind of CroqueMr/libreelec-x86-DV
issue #26 (skull-01; found by SamuriHL). Unchanged in libbluray master
f33a738fd7bb.
---
 .../org/videolan/media/content/playlist/PiPControlImpl.java     | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/PiPControlImpl.java b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/PiPControlImpl.java
index 042b5a1..5aeca74 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/PiPControlImpl.java
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/PiPControlImpl.java
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ public class PiPControlImpl extends VideoControl implements PiPControl, Asynchro
         } else {
             Dimension vd = getInputVideoSize();
             Dimension sd = getScreenSize();
-            setVideoArea(new HScreenRectangle(0.5f, 0.5f, vd.width / sd.width, vd.height / sd.height));
+            setVideoArea(new HScreenRectangle(0.5f, 0.5f, (float)vd.width / sd.width, (float)vd.height / sd.height));
         }
     }
 
